&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Commercial Account Executive, Mid-Market, Belgium &amp;amp; Luxembourg&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote | Hiring in the Netherlands or France&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. More than 50 million registered users, and more than half of the Fortune 100, trust us to ship better, more secure software faster. We’re all-remote, with a public handbook, a high-performance culture and a values-led way of working. This is a place where careers accelerate, and where you’ll work with sharp people who care about customers and getting things done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Belgium and Luxembourg are a great market for GitLab: a dense mix of fast-growing, engineering-led mid-sized companies, all modernizing how they plan, build, secure and ship software. As Mid-Market AE, you’ll own the territory end to end, from first conversation to close to long-term adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work alongside Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Customer Success, Renewals and Partners. Together you’ll use value-based selling (MEDDPICC and Command of the Message) to build pipeline, forecast accurately and grow GitLab’s footprint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location and language&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Covers Belgium and Luxembourg, but &lt;strong&gt;you must be based in the Netherlands or France.&lt;/strong&gt; We can’t hire for this role in Belgium itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent &lt;strong&gt;Dutch and English, or French and English.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular travel within the territory to meet customers and attend events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Mid-Market book of business in Belgium and Luxembourg, new and expansion, as the CEO of your territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pipeline through consistent prospecting and run disciplined, well-documented sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show customers the value of GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform to both business and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Customer Success, Renewals and our Partner ecosystem to win and grow accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption, prevent churn and forecast accurately against your quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host and attend regional events to build relationships with customers and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share win/loss learnings, improve our sales handbook, and be the voice of the customer in our public issue tracker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevOps, DevSecOps, Security, Software or SaaS sales experience, with a track record of value-based selling to business and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Dutch and English, or French and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery, negotiation and closing skills, plus comfort with outbound prospecting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine desire to see customers succeed with GitLab, and an interest in open source and developer tooling (Git, DevOps or ALM experience is a bonus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to meet customers in person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with GitLab’s values: Collaboration, Results for Customers, Efficiency, Diversity, Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging, Iteration, and Transparency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join GitLab’s Sales organization as part of a distributed team of Account Executives, Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Renewals and Partner colleagues. We work asynchronously and share playbooks and best practices in the handbook. You’ll get structure and support, and the autonomy to run your territory your way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How GitLab supports you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive on-target earnings with uncapped incentive pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity and Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;True all-remote working, wherever you’re most fulfilled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Many successful candidates don’t meet every requirement on paper. If you’re excited about this role, apply and let our recruiters take a look.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At IMC, technology is not a department; it&#39;s at the heart of everything we do. Developed in-house, our innovative software makes millions of trading decisions daily, and we win by making better and faster decisions than our competition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IMC&#39;s Amsterdam-based C++ Execution development teams work on software that sits directly in the latency-critical loop of our technology stack and touches every part of our organisation. We connect IMC to exchanges around the world, process massive volumes of market data in real time, execute complex trading algorithms, and integrate advanced hardware solutions where software alone isn&#39;t fast enough.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your Core Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer, you&#39;ll work in multidisciplinary teams alongside other engineers, traders, researchers, and quants, both locally and across our global offices, taking ownership of end-to-end product development, from requirements gathering to production. You&#39;ll write reliable, high-performance software while balancing time to production with quality and testability. Advanced automated testing lets us deploy to production daily. Within a complex landscape of varying systems and technologies, you&#39;ll be constantly challenged to consider trade-offs between latency, throughput, simplicity, scalability and maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-local-id=&quot;fbec03d6-4978-45ed-bbaf-55be803c5e72&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;bulletList&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building and maintaining the systems that connect IMC to exchanges: parsing market data feed, managing order entry, and keeping us fast and reliable on the path where latency counts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Implementing and optimising execution logic in close collaboration with traders and quants, translating trading ideas into production code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working with our hardware teams to integrate FPGA-based systems and low-latency network solutions into our trading stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Measuring, profiling and improving the performance of our systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Developing expertise across the entire software development lifecycle, learning from experienced engineers along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your Skills and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-local-id=&quot;a45fb6a2-e544-4212-81ca-57076957cb36&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;bulletList&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2-3 years of full-time professional work experience&lt;strong&gt; post-graduation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree&amp;nbsp;in Engineering, Computer Science or a related field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of algorithms and data structures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid programming skills in modern C++ (C++17 or later)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An interest in how software actually runs on hardware: memory, caches, networking&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A high degree of flexibility and adaptability: willing and able to deal with uncertainty and ambiguity in a rapidly evolving environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to solve problems creatively and proactively&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Curiosity and a willingness to learn. Interest in financial markets; previous knowledge is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Strength in Trust&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;OneTrust’s mission is to enable innovation through the responsible use of data and AI. We believe that ensuring data is trusted shouldn’t slow teams down—it should accelerate what’s possible. This led us to develop the first technology platform for responsible data use in 2016. Today, with AI representing the latest and most impactful expansion of data yet, OneTrust is once again redefining what responsible innovation looks like. OneTrust, the AI‑Ready Governance Platform™, unifies regulatory intelligence, automation, and connected governance workflows so businesses can continue to move at the speed of AI while ensuring good governance to prevent data misuse at scale. Trusted by thousands of organizations worldwide, OneTrust is shaping the future where trusted data becomes a transformative force for business and society.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE CHALLENGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Sr. Solutions Engineer&amp;nbsp;(SE) that will report to the Solutions Engineering Manager. In this role, you will drive business development and sales growth by providing technical expertise, competitive positioning, and product evaluation support to prospective customers for the OneTrust Data Privacy Compliance platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Serve as technical expert on systems integrations during major sales opportunities, including the preparation and delivery of proposals, RFPs and custom proof-of-concepts evaluations to demonstrate OneTrust’s integration capabilities to meet client objectives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Instrumental in technical deep dive discussions to architect integrations and advice customers on best practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Support Sales Teams with client meetings, presentations, and custom integration design options&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Coordinates with internal R&amp;amp;D, technical integrations, partner integrations teams to stay on top of product capabilities as well as future direction&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Conduct custom proof-of-concepts evaluations to demonstrate OneTrust’s integration capabilities to meet client objectives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Drive Sales and Marketing efforts in production of high-quality sales proposals and supporting assets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Maintain all sales cycle activities within the Salesforce.com CRM system&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have a clear understanding of the privacy industry, including regulatory environment, and will use this knowledge to support all of the primary responsibilities. To thrive in this role, you will keep up with industry trends, competitive landscape and customer needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR EXPERIENCE INCLUDES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &amp;nbsp; Native or fluent German/Dutch required;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &amp;nbsp; 4+ years of relevant experience, ideally in the technology industry and/or an Enterprise Cloud-based Software company;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Expertise selling, configuring and delivering software demonstrations;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Advanced knowledge of web applications, SaaS architecture, cloud computing and programming;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Expertise with implementing software products or solutions to enterprise companies;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;· &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Hands-on experience working with REST APIs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;·&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Familiarity with technologies such as JavaScript, FreeMarker, HTML, CSS, PowerShell, ASP.NET, C#, Kubernetes, Docker, or OpenShift is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Ability to build relationships across stakeholders in R&amp;amp;D, marketing, sales and engineering;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Strong entrepreneurial skills to excel in a complex and rapidly evolving environment;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Willingness to travel, as job requires (Estimated 25%);&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;BA/BS in Computer Science, Engineering or equivalent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;Where we Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are embracing an office-first culture, encouraging three days a week in office for most roles, with meaningful opportunities to collaborate and celebrate in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each role may have specific requirements or flexibility depending on the scope of the position, so we encourage you to verify this with your recruiter during your first interview.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;As an employee at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;OneTrust&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;, you will be part of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;OneTeam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;. That means &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt;you’ll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW202854797 BCX0&quot;&gt; receive support physically, mentally, and emotionally so that you can do your best work both in and out of the office. This includes comprehensive healthcare coverage, flexible PTO, equity RSUs, annual performance bonus opportunities, retirement account support, 14+ weeks of paid parental leave, career development opportunities, company-paid privacy certification exam fees, and much more. Specific benefits differ by country. For more information, talk to your recruiter or visit onetrust.com/careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
